{"step_index":146,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T07:32:28Z","input_tokens":2105,"cache_read_tokens":357876,"output_tokens":1348,"thinking":"The reported save time of 2.69 seconds for a .blend file with 679 total objects seems unexpectedly fast, warranting further investigation to ensure data integrity. The presence of zero FX camera raycast hits also needs to be contextualized within the scene setup to understand if this is an expected or problematic result. I will examine the scene structure to understand why the save is so rapid and the raycast results.\n\n\nThe rapid save times across different scenes are consistent, suggesting an underlying efficiency. Comparing save times across multiple scenes provides a baseline for investigating the unexpected speed. Now focusing on visual quality, a detailed audit will be conducted to assess luminance, color separation, halftone contrast, and ink outline integrity across rendered previews.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_board","args":{"since":27}},{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"import os\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageFilter\n\nPROJ = r\"D:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\"\nPDIR = os.path.join(PROJ, \"renders_v6\", \"preview\")\n\nprint(\"=== V6 SPIDER-VERSE PREVIEW QUANTITATIVE AUDIT ===\")\nfor fn in sorted(os.listdir(PDIR)):\n    if not fn.endswith(\".jpg\"):\n        continue\n    fp = os.path.join(PDIR, fn)\n    im = Image.open(fp).convert(\"RGB\")\n    arr = np.asarray(im, dtype=np.float32) / 255.0\n    blur = np.asarray(im.filter(ImageFilter.BoxBlur(3)), dtype=np.float32) / 255.0\n    lum = 0.2126 * arr[:, :, 0] + 0.7152 * arr[:, :, 1] + 0.0722 * arr[:, :, 2]\n    sat = arr.max(axis=2) - arr.min(axis=2)\n    # High-frequency halftone / crosshatch / ink detail energy in lower 72% (car + track)\n    H, W = lum.shape\n    fg = np.abs(arr[int(H * 0.28) :] - blur[int(H * 0.28) :]).mean() * 255.0\n    ink_pct = float((lum < 0.035).mean() * 100.0)\n    clip_pct = float((lum > 0.985).mean() * 100.0)\n    sky_rgb = arr[: int(H * 0.28)].mean(axis=(0, 1)).round(3)\n    fg_rgb = arr[int(H * 0.35) :].mean(axis=(0, 1)).round(3)\n    print(\n        f\"{fn:32s} | mean={lum.mean():.3f} p05={np.percentile(lum,5):.3f} p95={np.percentile(lum,95):.3f} \"\n        f\"| sat={sat.mean():.3f} | clip={clip_pct:.2f}% | ink<0.035={ink_pct:.2f}% \"\n        f\"| HF_detail={fg:.2f}/255 | skyRGB={sky_rgb} fgRGB={fg_rgb}\"\n    )\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\b13776a0-7d9f-4f63-9e67-c8ecc5f11412\\scratch\\verify_v6_previews.py"}},{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python \"C:\\Users\\86052\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\b13776a0-7d9f-4f63-9e67-c8ecc5f11412\\scratch\\verify_v6_previews.py\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolSummary":"Verify V6 Spider-Verse preview PIL metrics"}}]}
